New LLD Problem: Elevator System

Assume you've never designed it before.

Interview prompt

Design an Elevator System for a building.

The building has multiple floors and multiple elevators.

The system should allow:

A user to request an elevator from a floor.
A user inside an elevator to select a destination floor.
Multiple elevators can exist in the building.
The system should decide which elevator should serve a request.
Elevator should move between floors.
Elevator should open and close its doors.
Elevator should maintain its current floor and direction.
The system should handle multiple elevator requests.

1. Functional requirements

we have multiple elivators
user press the button at particular floor
user press the button from inside to reach desire floor
if there are different button for different elevator pressed one will come
if not system to check whcih one to come
Eleveator move between the floor and automatilcally close and open dorr

2. Entities

Elevator -> id, currentFloor, isActive boolean, direction enum
Floor -> int number
Building -> id, name, List<Elevator> elevators, List<Floor>
Direction enum -> UP, DOWN, IDEL
ElivatorRequest -> sourceFloor, Direction
DestinationRequest -> id, destinationFloor
Request Enum -> pending completed

3. Relationships
building has floor 1 to many composition
building has elevator 1 to many association
ElevaorRequest has direction 1 to 1
destination has floor Number 1 to 1

4. Entity responsibilities

Elevator
    processElevatorRequest(ElevatorRequest)
    processDestinationRequest(DestinationRequest)

 Building
     markElevatorAcitve()
     markElevatorInActive()

ElevatorRequest
    markCompleted()
    markPending()

 DestiinationRequest
    markCompleted()
    markPending()
